.TH CORVUS 1 "2026-08-16" "corvus-cli 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
corvus \- command-line client for Corvus
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B corvus
.I <command>
.RI [ resource ]
.RI [ name ]
.I [flags]
.br
.B corvus
.B help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B corvus
is a command-line client for Corvus. It uses
the machine-facing
.BR /eso/v1
API for secret CRUD and the
.BR /api/v1/manage
API (personal access tokens) for teams, projects, members, groups, tokens,
trash, audit, and users.
.PP
Three token kinds are supported:
.TP
.B ss_...
Machine token. Scoped to one project; lists, reads, and writes secrets in
that project only, bypassing human reveal-approval and per-secret ACL.
Requires a project
.BR UUID .
.TP
.B pat_...
Personal access token. Acts as the owning user under RLS; can access any
team or project the user is a member of (by UUID or unique name) and can run
org and admin commands.
.TP
.B sso_...
CLI session token, minted by the web UI "Copy login command" flow and pasted
into a
.BR "corvus login"
command. User-scoped, short-lived (TTL set by the server), and behaves like
.IR pat_... .
.PP
With no arguments,
.B corvus
prints a usage summary and exits with status 0. The same summary is
available via
.BR "corvus\ help".
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B login, configure
.RB [ \-\-url URL \-\-token TOKEN [\-\-project PROJECT] ]
Store credentials for future runs.
.I \-\-project
is required only for
.IR ss_...
tokens.
.TP
.BI project " [ NAME ]"
Show the current default project, or switch to
.IR NAME
(name for a PAT or CLI session token, UUID for a machine token).
.TP
.BI "get " RESOURCE " [name]"
List or fetch a resource. See the RESOURCES section for valid values.
.TP
.BI "apply, set " "secret NAME [flags]"
Create or update a secret (value, note, kind, expiry, metadata, access mode).
.TP
.BI "create " RESOURCE
.RI NAME " [flags]"
Create a team, project, member, group, group-member, token, or secret.
.TP
.BI "delete " RESOURCE
.RI NAME " [flags]"
Delete a resource. Deleting a team, project, or trashed secret (purge)
requires
.BR \-\-yes .
.TP
.BI "reveal " "secret NAME [--reason TEXT]"
Request reveal approval (or print the value with
.BR \-o\ value ).
.TP
.BI "approve|deny " ID
.RI [ \-\-minutes N ]
Resolve a pending reveal access request. Allowed grant durations: 15, 60,
240, 1440 minutes.
.TP
.BI "restore trash " ID |"
.B restore trash --all
Restore one soft-deleted secret, or all.
.TP
.BI "transfer team " NAME " --email " USER
Transfer team ownership to USER .
.TP
.BI "grant secret " NAME
.RB [ \-\-to EMAIL | \-\-group ID | \-\-sa TOKEN_ID ]
.RB [ \-\-role ROLETH ]
Add a secret-scope role binding (project admin).
.TP
.BI "unbind secret " NAME " " BINDING_ID
Remove a secret-scope role binding.
.TP
.BI "export " [ PROJECT ]
.RB [ \-o\ env|json|csv|value|table ]
Export project secrets as plaintext (audited).
.TP
.BI settings
.RB [ " --require-reveal-approval\ on|off " ]
.RB [ " --default-access-mode inherit|restricted " ]
.RB [ " --description TEXT " ]
Update project settings (project admin).
.TP
.B ssh
.RB [ setup | list | status | sync | uninstall ]
Native
.BR ssh (1)
to Corvus hosts. Requires
.BR ssh-agent (1) .
See
.BR SSH
below.
.SH RESOURCES
The
.BR get
command accepts these resources:
.TP
.BR secrets
List secret metadata for the current project.
.TP
.BR secret
\fINAME\fR
Fetch a single secret by key (path-style keys with / are allowed).
.TP
.BR projects |, \fBproject \fINAME
List projects, or show one.
.TP
.BR teams | team
.RB [ NAME ]
List teams, or show one.
.TP
.BR members | member
List current project members, or with
.B \-\-team T
team members.
.TP
.BR tokens | token
List machine tokens for the current project.
.TP
.BR groups
with
.B \-\-team T
list groups of a team.
.TP
.BR trash
List soft-deleted secrets.
.TP
.BR history
\fBNAME\fR
Show version history of a secret.
.TP
.BR requests
List access requests
.RB ( --status pending|approved|denied|all ).
.TP
.BR audit
.RB [ \-\-source project|org|secret|access ]
Show secret or org audit.
.TP
.BR users
List users (global admin, PAT or CLI session token).
.PP
The
.BR create
and
.BR delete
commands accept: team, project, member, group, group-member, token, trash,
and secret.
.SH OPTIONS
Most subcommands accept a subset of the following:
.TP
.BI \-o , \-\-output FORMAT
Output format: table (default), json, value, name, wide.
.TP
.BI \-\-project PROJECT
Project reference: UUID, or unique name for a PAT or CLI session token.
.TP
.BI \-\-team TEAM
Team reference for team-scoped resources.
.TP
.BI \-\-scope K1, GLOB
Key allow-list passed to
.B create token
(exact keys and/or globs; comma- or space-separated).
.TP
.BI \-\-from-file PATH
Read the secret value from a file ( \fB\-\fR = stdin).
.TP
.BI \-\-from-env VAR
Read the secret value from an environment variable.
.TP
.BI \-\-value VALUE
Literal secret value (avoid in interactive shells; use
.BR \-\-from-file
or
.BR \-\-from-env ).
.TP
.BI \-\-note TEXT
Attach a note to a secret.
.TP
.BI \-\-kind KIND
Secret kind: plain, database, certificate, ssh, kv.
.TP
.BI \-\-expires\-days N
Set expiry N days from now.
.TP
.BR \-\-clear\-expires
Clear a secret's expiry.
.TP
.BI \-\-meta KEY=VALUE
Set one custom metadata field (repeatable; PAT required).
.TP
.BI \-\-delete\-meta KEY
Remove one custom metadata field (PAT required).
.TP
.BI \-\-access\-mode MODE
Set a secret's access mode: inherit or restricted (project admin).
.TP
.BI \-\-requires\-approval on|off|inherit
Override reveal approval for a secret (project admin).
.TP
.BI \-\-project PROJECT
Target a project by UUID or unique name (PAT) without switching the default.
.TP
.BR \-\-yes
Confirm a destructive delete (team, project, or trash purge). Without it the
command refuses and exits.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SS_URL
Base URL of the server (no trailing slash).
.TP
.B SS_TOKEN
Token: ss_... , pat_..., or sso_....
.TP
.B SS_PROJECT
Default project (UUID, or name with a
.I pat_...
or
.IR sso_...
token). Alias:
.BR PID .
.PP
Environment variables take precedence over the config file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/corvus/config
Configuration file, mode 0600, written by
.BR "corvus login".
.TP
.B ~/.ssh/config.d/corvus
Generated OpenSSH Include fragment
.RB ( "corvus ssh setup" / "corvus ssh sync" ).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
List secrets:
.B corvus get secrets
.TP
Get one secret as a raw value:
.B corvus get secret API_KEY \-o value
.TP
History-safe write from stdin:
.B printf '%s' "$NEW" | corvus apply secret API_KEY --from-file=-
.TP
Create a team and project:
.B corvus create team Platform
.br
.B corvus create project demo --team Platform
.TP
Create a write token scoped to two keys:
.B corvus create token ci --role service-write --scope 'API_KEY,prod/*'
.TP
Restrict a secret and grant a user:
.B corvus apply secret API_KEY --access-mode restricted
.br
.B corvus grant secret API_KEY --to alice@example.com --role secret-reveal
.TP
Export secrets:
.B corvus export --output env
.TP
SSH hosts (requires ssh-agent):
.B corvus ssh setup
.br
.B ssh web01
.SH SSH
.B corvus ssh
wires native
.BR ssh (1)
to Corvus
.B kind=ssh
secrets. Private keys are loaded into
.BR ssh-agent (1)
on first connect
.RB ( ssh-add \-t );
only
.B .pub
files are written locally.
.PP
Subcommands:
.BR setup
(install Include and discover hosts),
.BR list ,
.BR status ,
.BR sync
.RB [ \-\-eager ],
.BR uninstall
.RB [ \-\-purge ].
.PP
An agent must be reachable at
.BR SSH_AUTH_SOCK .
On Fedora and current RHEL, install the client and enable the user socket shipped by
.BR openssh-clients :
.PP
.nf
sudo dnf install -y openssh-clients
systemctl --user enable --now ssh-agent.socket
export SSH_AUTH_SOCK="${XDG_RUNTIME_DIR}/ssh-agent.socket"
.fi
.PP
Add that
.B export
to
.B ~/.bashrc
so login shells see the socket. The systemd unit does not export
.B SSH_AUTH_SOCK
into interactive shells by itself (KDE Plasma does via
.BR /etc/xdg/plasma-workspace/env/ssh-agent.sh ).
.PP
If
.B systemctl --user cat ssh-agent.socket
fails (older RHEL 9), start an agent in the current shell:
.PP
.nf
eval "$(ssh-agent -s)"
.fi
.PP
GNOME Workstation may already provide an agent via GNOME Keyring. Prefer the
OpenSSH agent so
.B ssh-add \-t
(Corvus TTL) is honoured. See the README section
.B ssh-agent on Fedora / RHEL
for environment.d, verification with
.B ssh-add \-l
and
.BR "corvus ssh status" .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on failure (missing credentials, HTTP error, invalid input).
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation is in the project's README, and the API reference in the
server repository at
.BR corvus/docs/dev/api.md .
.SH BUGS
Report issues to the project repository.